/Title (Classification of Complex Financial Instruments: Division II adopts a substance-over-form approach to financial instruments. Under Ind AS 32, management must assess whether an instrument is equity or a financial liability based on its contractual terms, particularly for instruments such as redeemable preference shares. Further, compound instruments like convertible debentures are required to be bifurcated into equity and liability components for presentation, with measurement guided by Ind AS 109.)
